diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/P10-LAUNCH-GATES.md b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/P10-LAUNCH-GATES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..495b6e7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/P10-LAUNCH-GATES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# P10 production admission boundary
+
+P10 adds an executable denial boundary to the candidate's real `main.cc`.
+`SONGPLUS_P10_INTEGRATION` is enabled by the candidate SConscript. The default
+entry returns 3 before logging, real-time setup, `Hardware` queries, discovery,
+or the legacy SPI constructor. There is no native production launcher or
+production evidence verifier in this stage. An unknown physical profile remains
+UNBOUND; neither an environment variable nor a JSON field can unlock startup.
+
+The existing explicit `--compat-offline` and `--compat-runtime-offline` tests
+remain available. New `--compat-production-check-offline` returns 0 when the
+inert default check correctly reports blocked admission. Its success is success
+of a diagnostic, never authorization to start. It performs no device discovery,
+file/config loading, kernel I/O, control writes, CAN transmission, or installation.
+Unsupported `--compat-*` arguments still return 2.
+The offline acceptance executes the SConscript build contract and manually links
+the actual Linux daemon entry; it does not claim an actual full SCons build.
+
+## Review is separate from authority
+
+`evaluate_production_gate` is a pure readiness evaluator. It always returns
+false for device access, runtime writes, CAN TX, deployment and production start
+authorization, even when injected synthetic evidence satisfies every check.
+This makes an offline positive test useful without manufacturing a deployment
+capability. P10 does not implement post-handoff admission or continuous
+revocation of production authority.
+
+| Requested review | Required evidence, in addition to the preceding row |
+| --- | --- |
+| Offline diagnostics | No hardware evidence; every authority remains false. |
+| Native read-only observation | Valid native binding, locked release, physical identity, recovery chain, power/topology, exclusive ownership, peripheral roles, bounded discovery scheduling and kernel I/O deadline evidence. USB also needs the current active interface; SPI needs configuration and cross-process freshness. |
+| Native noOutput runtime | Resource bounds, complete-group health/safety barrier, heartbeat and shutdown behavior. This purpose is a bench review, not driver assistance. |
+| Vehicle control | Working driver monitoring, audible alerts, validated vehicle signals/controller, independent Panda safety and closed-course results. |
+| Deployment | Installation and rollback evidence. The default production diagnostic requests this full scope. |
+
+Evidence references have bounded shape, unique requirement IDs and short-lived
+attestation windows. The verifier must read the referenced content and associate
+it with the entire current context: exact board/MCU/capability/role tuple, full
+application signatures, release lock, process epoch, discovery revision and
+retained leases. A digest, a `true` value, an offline report or a caller-supplied
+timestamp is not verification. No real verifier is supplied by P10. Historical
+physical evidence may be re-attested for a current session only after this
+association is independently verified; acquisition times must remain intact.
+
+Both board observations must be real completed-probe timestamps, no older than
+the locked `kLoopMaxGapUs` value (250,000 us), and neither may be future-dated.
+The evaluator never re-stamps stale evidence. Every new evaluation re-runs the
+verifiers; there is no cached success. A previous review result is unusable after
+handoff, ownership/process/revision changes, retirement or cancellation.
+
+## SPI live proof
+
+The serialized executor supplies `LiveSpiProofReader` for each fixed SPI slot.
+It must call `SpiFreshnessBackend::proof()` on the still-owned, live backend;
+copied JSON or a saved discovery result cannot replace this operation. The gate
+checks the expected UID and lease nonce, two distinct nonzero fence IDs, actual
+fence completion time and the still-held same-fd lifetime flock. The current
+process/revision/context is also passed to the callback and evidence verifier.
+Missing callbacks, owner retirement and exceptions deny review.
+
+An old fence can remain valid while the same descriptor and exclusive lock are
+continuously held; the board identity observations must still be re-probed on
+schedule. A local cancellation invalidates proof. The fence proves behavior only
+under the locked firmware's one-entry `(request ID, CRC)` cache and cooperative
+ownership of every master using that physical SPI node. It does not prove target
+kernel deadlines, physical identity, power stability or absence of an unrelated
+master. The proof's `kernel_deadline_proven` remains false and cannot substitute
+for independently verified timing evidence.
+
+## Remaining physical work
+
+Before considering any actual native startup, verify the two physical identities,
+board/firmware/ABI and topology, safe recovery, current USB interface or exact SPI
+node/configuration, exclusive ownership, target worst-case I/O latency and worker
+cleanup. Verify resource/stack bounds, health/safety and heartbeat/exit faults.
+Vehicle operation additionally requires a driver-monitoring solution (the C3XL's
+missing camera is not a bypass), audible alerts, independently confirmed Song
+PLUS signals/controller/safety and controlled validation. Passing the offline
+matrix supplies none of these physical facts.
diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/discovery_scheduler.cc b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/discovery_scheduler.cc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3b2c36c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/discovery_scheduler.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,164 @@
+#include "discovery_scheduler.h"
+
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <limits>
+
+namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility {
+namespace {
+bool add(std::uint64_t a, std::uint64_t b, std::uint64_t &out) {
+  if (b > UINT64_MAX-a) return false;
+  out=a+b; return true;
+}
+bool same_item(const DiscoveryItem &a, const DiscoveryItem &b) {
+  return a.identity==b.identity && a.handle_nonce==b.handle_nonce &&
+    a.usb_alt0_verified==b.usb_alt0_verified && a.spi_first_request_id==b.spi_first_request_id;
+}
+bool valid_nonce(const std::string &s) {
+  return !s.empty() && s.size()<=128 && std::all_of(s.begin(),s.end(),[](unsigned char c){return c>32 && c<127;});
+}
+}
+
+DiscoveryScheduler::DiscoveryScheduler(const SessionProfile &profile, Clock &clock, DiscoveryTaskProvider &provider,
+                                       DiscoveryCommitSink &sink, DiscoveryScheduleConfig config)
+  : profile_(profile), config_(config), clock_(clock), provider_(provider), sink_(sink) {
+  try { const SessionRegistry validated(profile_); (void)validated; }
+  catch (...) { reason_="INVALID_PROFILE"; return; }
+  if (!config_.allow_scheduling || (profile_.binding_status!="SYNTHETIC_BOUND" && profile_.binding_status!="NATIVE_READ_ONLY_BOUND")) return;
+  if (!config_.reprobe_interval_us || !config_.task_timeout_us || !config_.max_observation_age_us ||
+      config_.max_observation_age_us>kLoopMaxGapUs ||
+      config_.reprobe_interval_us>=config_.max_observation_age_us ||
+      config_.task_timeout_us>=config_.max_observation_age_us-config_.reprobe_interval_us ||
+      !config_.initial_backoff_us || config_.maximum_backoff_us<config_.initial_backoff_us ||
+      config_.maximum_backoff_us>10000000 || !config_.callback_budget_us || config_.callback_budget_us>kLoopBudgetUs) {
+    reason_="INVALID_SCHEDULE_CONFIG"; return;
+  }
+  state_=DiscoveryScheduleState::Waiting; reason_="AWAITING_COMPLETE_DISCOVERY"; backoff_us_=config_.initial_backoff_us;
+}
+DiscoveryScheduler::~DiscoveryScheduler() { stop(); }
+bool DiscoveryScheduler::read_clock(std::uint64_t &now) noexcept {
+  try { now=clock_.now_us(); }
+  catch (...) { return false; }
+  if (!now || (clock_seen_ && now<last_clock_)) return false;
+  last_clock_=now; clock_seen_=true; return true;
+}
+void DiscoveryScheduler::retire(const char *reason, DiscoveryTickResult *tick) noexcept {
+  const bool affected=task_ || !snapshot_.items.empty();
+  snapshot_={}; slot_observed_us_={};
+  // The sink revokes runtime epochs before any cancellation can wake a worker
+  // that owns native leases. Otherwise cleanup could race a still-live epoch.
+  if (affected) { sink_.retire(reason); if (tick) tick->retired=true; }
+  if (task_) { task_->cancel(); task_.reset(); }
+}
+void DiscoveryScheduler::fail(const char *reason, std::uint64_t now, bool terminal, DiscoveryTickResult *tick) noexcept {
+  retire(reason,tick); reason_=reason;
+  if (terminal || !add(now,backoff_us_,due_us_)) { state_=DiscoveryScheduleState::Failed; return; }
+  state_=DiscoveryScheduleState::Backoff;
+  // Saturating exponential retry, never an overflow or an immediate busy loop.
+  backoff_us_=backoff_us_>config_.maximum_backoff_us/2 ? config_.maximum_backoff_us :
+    std::min(config_.maximum_backoff_us,backoff_us_*2);
+}
+bool DiscoveryScheduler::callback_time(std::uint64_t before, std::uint64_t &after, DiscoveryTickResult &tick) {
+  if (!read_clock(after)) { fail("CLOCK_INVALID",before,true,&tick); return false; }
+  if (after-before>config_.callback_budget_us) { fail("NONBLOCKING_CALLBACK_BUDGET_EXCEEDED",after,true,&tick); return false; }
+  return true;
+}
+bool DiscoveryScheduler::validate(const DiscoveryTaskResult &result, std::uint64_t now, const char *&reason) const {
+  const auto reject=[&](const char *why) { reason=why; return false; };
+  const auto &s=result.snapshot;
+  if (result.generation!=request_.generation || result.kind!=request_.kind) return reject("STALE_TASK_COMPLETION");
+  if (!s.revision || s.revision<=last_revision_) return reject("DISCOVERY_REVISION_NOT_NEW");
+  if (s.items.size()!=2) return reject("COMPLETE_TWO_BOARD_GROUP_REQUIRED");
+  std::array<const DiscoveryItem *,2> items{};
+  for (const auto &item:s.items) {
+    const auto slot=item.identity.identity==profile_.slots[0].expected.identity ? 0U:1U;
+    if (!(item.identity==profile_.slots[slot].expected) || items[slot] || !valid_nonce(item.handle_nonce)) return reject("IDENTITY_OR_HANDLE_MISMATCH");
+    if (item.identity.transport=="USB" ? (!item.usb_alt0_verified || item.spi_first_request_id) :
+        item.identity.transport=="SPI" ? (item.usb_alt0_verified || !item.spi_first_request_id) : true)
+      return reject("ACTIVATION_EVIDENCE_MISSING");
+    items[slot]=&item;
+  }
+  if (!items[0] || !items[1] || items[0]->handle_nonce==items[1]->handle_nonce) return reject("DUPLICATE_OR_MISSING_HANDLE");
+  if (s.observed_us!=std::min(result.slot_observed_us[0],result.slot_observed_us[1])) return reject("ORIGINAL_PROBE_TIME_REQUIRED");
+  for (std::size_t slot=0;slot<2;++slot) {
+    const auto stamp=result.slot_observed_us[slot];
+    if (!stamp || stamp<request_.started_us || stamp>now || now-stamp>=config_.max_observation_age_us)
+      return reject("PROBE_TIME_INVALID_OR_STALE");
+    if (request_.kind==DiscoveryTaskKind::Reprobe) {
+      const auto previous=std::find_if(snapshot_.items.begin(),snapshot_.items.end(),[&](const auto &item){return item.identity.identity==items[slot]->identity.identity;});
+      if (previous==snapshot_.items.end() || !same_item(*previous,*items[slot])) return reject("REPROBE_CHANGED_RETAINED_HANDLE");
+      if (stamp<=slot_observed_us_[slot]) return reject("REPROBE_DID_NOT_ADVANCE_EVIDENCE");
+    } else if (consumed_.count(items[slot]->handle_nonce)) return reject("RETIRED_HANDLE_REUSED");
+  }
+  if (request_.kind==DiscoveryTaskKind::Discover && consumed_.size()>126) return reject("HANDLE_HISTORY_EXHAUSTED");
+  return true;
+}
+DiscoveryTickResult DiscoveryScheduler::tick() {
+  DiscoveryTickResult out;
+  const auto finish=[&] { out.state=state_; out.reason=reason_; return out; };
+  if (state_==DiscoveryScheduleState::Denied || state_==DiscoveryScheduleState::Stopped || state_==DiscoveryScheduleState::Failed) return finish();
+  std::uint64_t now=0;
+  if (!read_clock(now)) { fail("CLOCK_INVALID",last_clock_,true,&out); return finish(); }
+  if (invalidated_) { invalidated_=false; fail("EXTERNAL_GROUP_INVALIDATED",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+  if (!snapshot_.items.empty() && (snapshot_.observed_us>now || now-snapshot_.observed_us>=config_.max_observation_age_us)) {
+    fail("GROUP_OBSERVATION_EXPIRED",now,false,&out); return finish();
+  }
+  if (task_) {
+    if (now>=request_.deadline_us) { fail("DISCOVERY_TASK_TIMEOUT",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+    DiscoveryPollResult poll;
+    try { out.polled=true; poll=task_->poll(); }
+    catch (...) { fail("DISCOVERY_POLL_EXCEPTION",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+    if (!callback_time(now,now,out)) return finish();
+    if (now>=request_.deadline_us) { fail("DISCOVERY_TASK_TIMEOUT",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+    if (poll.state==DiscoveryPollState::Pending) return finish();
+    if (poll.state!=DiscoveryPollState::Complete) { fail("DISCOVERY_TASK_FAILED",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+    const char *invalid="INVALID_DISCOVERY_RESULT";
+    if (!validate(poll.result,now,invalid)) {
+      fail(invalid,now,std::string(invalid)=="HANDLE_HISTORY_EXHAUSTED",&out); return finish();
+    }
+    // Consume leases before handoff, including a failed/throwing handoff.
+    if (request_.kind==DiscoveryTaskKind::Discover) for (const auto &item:poll.result.snapshot.items) consumed_.insert(item.handle_nonce);
+    last_revision_=poll.result.snapshot.revision;
+    auto accepted_snapshot=poll.result.snapshot;
+    const auto accepted_stamps=poll.result.slot_observed_us;
+    bool committed=false;
+    try { committed=sink_.commit(request_,poll.result); }
+    catch (...) { fail("DISCOVERY_COMMIT_EXCEPTION",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+    if (!callback_time(now,now,out)) return finish();
+    if (!committed) { fail("DISCOVERY_COMMIT_REJECTED",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+    if (now>=request_.deadline_us || now-accepted_snapshot.observed_us>=config_.max_observation_age_us) {
+      fail("DISCOVERY_HANDOFF_EXPIRED",now,false,&out); return finish();
+    }
+    task_.reset();
+    snapshot_=std::move(accepted_snapshot); slot_observed_us_=accepted_stamps;
+    // Schedule from actual oldest evidence, not the time a mailbox was polled.
+    if (!add(snapshot_.observed_us,config_.reprobe_interval_us,due_us_)) {
+      fail("SCHEDULE_COUNTER_EXHAUSTED",now,true,&out); return finish();
+    }
+    backoff_us_=config_.initial_backoff_us;
+    state_=DiscoveryScheduleState::Ready; reason_="COMPLETE_GROUP_EVIDENCE_CURRENT"; out.committed=true;
+    return finish();
+  }
+  if (now<due_us_) return finish();
+  if (next_generation_==UINT64_MAX || !add(now,config_.task_timeout_us,request_.deadline_us)) {
+    fail("SCHEDULE_COUNTER_EXHAUSTED",now,true,&out); return finish();
+  }
+  request_.generation=++next_generation_; request_.started_us=now; request_.previous=snapshot_;
+  request_.kind=snapshot_.items.empty() ? DiscoveryTaskKind::Discover:DiscoveryTaskKind::Reprobe;
+  try { out.started=true; task_=provider_.start(request_); }
+  catch (...) { fail("DISCOVERY_START_EXCEPTION",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+  if (!callback_time(now,now,out)) return finish();
+  if (!task_) { fail("DISCOVERY_WORKER_UNAVAILABLE",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+  if (now>=request_.deadline_us) { fail("DISCOVERY_TASK_TIMEOUT",now,false,&out); return finish(); }
+  state_=request_.kind==DiscoveryTaskKind::Discover ? DiscoveryScheduleState::Discovering:DiscoveryScheduleState::Reprobing;
+  reason_=request_.kind==DiscoveryTaskKind::Discover ? "COMPLETE_DISCOVERY_PENDING":"RETAINED_HANDLE_REPROBE_PENDING";
+  return finish();
+}
+void DiscoveryScheduler::stop() noexcept {
+  if (state_==DiscoveryScheduleState::Stopped) return;
+  retire("SCHEDULER_STOPPED"); state_=DiscoveryScheduleState::Stopped; reason_="SCHEDULER_STOPPED";
+}
+void DiscoveryScheduler::invalidate() noexcept {
+  if (state_==DiscoveryScheduleState::Denied || state_==DiscoveryScheduleState::Stopped || state_==DiscoveryScheduleState::Failed) return;
+  retire("EXTERNAL_GROUP_INVALIDATED"); invalidated_=true;
+}
+}  // namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility
diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/discovery_scheduler.h b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/discovery_scheduler.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..de7dd3f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/discovery_scheduler.h
@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@
+#pragma once
+
+#include <memory>
+#include "runtime_integration.h"
+
+namespace openpilot::pandad::compatibility {
+
+enum class DiscoveryTaskKind { Discover, Reprobe };
+struct DiscoveryTaskRequest {
+  std::uint64_t generation = 0, started_us = 0, deadline_us = 0;
+  DiscoveryTaskKind kind = DiscoveryTaskKind::Discover;
+  DiscoverySnapshot previous;
+};
+// Ownership transfer only. Destruction must enqueue native cleanup, never join
+// a worker or synchronously wait for kernel I/O on the owner thread.
+struct DiscoveryTaskPayload { virtual ~DiscoveryTaskPayload() = default; };
+struct DiscoveryTaskResult {
+  std::uint64_t generation = 0;
+  DiscoveryTaskKind kind = DiscoveryTaskKind::Discover;
+  DiscoverySnapshot snapshot;
+  // Fixed profile slot order, independently of snapshot.items order. These are
+  // actual completed identity reads, never scheduler/handoff timestamps.
+  std::array<std::uint64_t,2> slot_observed_us{};
+  std::unique_ptr<DiscoveryTaskPayload> payload;
+};
+enum class DiscoveryPollState { Pending, Complete, Failed };
+struct DiscoveryPollResult {
+  DiscoveryPollState state = DiscoveryPollState::Pending;
+  DiscoveryTaskResult result;
+};
+class DiscoveryTask {
+public:
+  virtual ~DiscoveryTask() = default;
+  // Nonblocking mailbox query. The worker does enumeration, probes and cleanup;
+  // it may not publish a lease directly or mutate the serialized runtime owner.
+  virtual DiscoveryPollResult poll() = 0;
+  virtual void cancel() noexcept = 0;  // local cancellation signal only
+};
+class DiscoveryTaskProvider {
+public:
+  virtual ~DiscoveryTaskProvider() = default;
+  // Nonblocking enqueue. One outstanding task per scheduler, no unbounded
+  // worker queue. A cancelled kernel call must retain its lane until it ends;
+  // start returns null while that lane is unavailable.
+  virtual std::unique_ptr<DiscoveryTask> start(const DiscoveryTaskRequest &) = 0;
+};
+class DiscoveryCommitSink {
+public:
+  virtual ~DiscoveryCommitSink() = default;
+  // Transfer already probed retained leases for Discover; Reprobe only updates
+  // same-handle evidence. Neither path reopens, claims, probes or performs I/O.
+  virtual bool commit(const DiscoveryTaskRequest &, DiscoveryTaskResult &) = 0;
+  // Revoke BOTH runtime epochs before releasing owners. No blocking cleanup.
+  virtual void retire(const char *reason) noexcept = 0;
+};
+struct DiscoveryScheduleConfig {
+  bool allow_scheduling = false;
+  std::uint64_t reprobe_interval_us = 50000;
+  std::uint64_t task_timeout_us = 100000;
+  std::uint64_t max_observation_age_us = kLoopMaxGapUs;
+  std::uint64_t initial_backoff_us = 10000, maximum_backoff_us = 500000;
+  std::uint64_t callback_budget_us = 1000;
+};
+enum class DiscoveryScheduleState { Denied, Waiting, Discovering, Ready, Reprobing, Backoff, Stopped, Failed };
+struct DiscoveryTickResult {
+  DiscoveryScheduleState state = DiscoveryScheduleState::Denied;
+  bool started = false, polled = false, committed = false, retired = false;
+  std::string reason = "UNBOUND_OR_SCHEDULING_DENIED";
+};
+
+// Serialized owner-thread state machine. Tick does at most one start OR poll
+// and never waits/sleeps. Health/heartbeat remain the caller's responsibility
+// each cycle, even while a discovery task is pending. Callback timing is only
+// checked after return; native hard-deadline proof is a separate production
+// gate. Supplying an asynchronous interface is not proof of such a deadline.
+class DiscoveryScheduler final : public DiscoveryProvider {
+public:
+  DiscoveryScheduler(const SessionProfile &, Clock &, DiscoveryTaskProvider &, DiscoveryCommitSink &,
+                     DiscoveryScheduleConfig = {});
+  ~DiscoveryScheduler();
+  DiscoveryScheduler(const DiscoveryScheduler &)=delete;
+  DiscoveryScheduler &operator=(const DiscoveryScheduler &)=delete;
+  DiscoveryScheduler(DiscoveryScheduler &&)=delete;
+  DiscoveryScheduler &operator=(DiscoveryScheduler &&)=delete;
+  DiscoveryTickResult tick();
+  void stop() noexcept;
+  // Runtime-side transport/health retirement also invalidates the scheduler's
+  // retained evidence. Reconnection must rediscover BOTH fresh handle leases.
